# flOW — functor contract (inspired by OCaml functors).
#
# In OCaml a functor is a module parameterized by another module:
#     module Make (Deps : S) : T = struct ... end
# A flOW functor is an object that builds a configured Module from the App
# context — reading the app's config and resolving services it depends on — and
# returns a ready-to-register module instance.
#
#   make(app) -> Module
#
# Register it with `app.apply(new MyFunctor())`, which calls make(app) and uses
# the result. This is how you parameterize a module (e.g. a starting value, a
# chosen backend, a wrapped/decorated module) without hardcoding it.
interface Functor:
  fn make(app)
